node_modules/
.dsh-home*/
*.tgz
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
LOCAL_CONTEXT.md

# Build output of the TypeScript packages. Never committed: `prepack` rebuilds it,
# so a published tarball always matches its source and there is no "did you
# remember to rebuild?" failure mode. `packages/probe/lib` is deliberately not
# covered — that one is hand-written source, not generated.
packages/*/lib/

# The write trail a local run leaves beside a domain. A domain pack is data, not part
# of this repository, but a fixture used as one would otherwise drop this next to the
# source.
.audit.jsonl

# Python (tools/fde)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Scratch: local probe output that must never be committed.
_*.txt
_*.json

# Any dsh run log. This was a list of exact names, and the second name was missed — so the file
# landed in the repository with a live session token in it. A glob states the rule instead of
# enumerating what happened to be there the day it was written.
dsh-*.log

# The sandbox own record of who wrote what. Like the audit trail, not domain data.
.provenance.jsonl

# The working record. Written as notes, in the language of the work, which means it keeps
# collecting internal project names and local paths — sanitising it was a losing game, and the
# file that says so is the file that broke the rule. Not published, so there is nothing to leak.
PROJECT_STATE.md

# Test output the capability writes. Its default command puts a junit report beside the tests it
# ran, and a run against the repository itself therefore leaves one here — a report naming the
# service, carrying every test name, and quoting the source of any test that failed. Found sitting
# untracked in the tree, one `git add -A` away from being published, which is the same shape of
# mistake as the run log this file already has a rule for: a tool's own output is not source.
qa-output*/
.junit.xml
